I've ascended two previous wizards, because wizards are about the only
class that interest me in themselves. (I've also ascended a valkyrie,
priest and rogue, but I keep abandoning barbarians in Gehennom because
I get bored.)

This wizard started with charm monster, and for the first time ever I
was confident  from the start that he would ascend. It was never even
close. One magic lamp got me SDSM, but everything else was a little
thin on the ground. I even teased some puddings into making enough
altar fodder to get crowned for my FOD spellbook.

I tried a few new things this time. I'd never trained Detect Monster to
skilled before. That was nice. And I finally saddled a dragon. That
wasn't as much fun as I thought it would be, and I quit after a couple
of levels.

I didn't beat Vlad to death with a carrot, but I'll try that next time.
That sounds like a new minor behavior, like converting all altars, or
not killing Itzhak.

